@startuml recruiter-outputs
title Use: a recruiter reviews matches fairly across archetypes (v2)

skinparam shadowing false

start
:Recruiter opens a job's candidate list\n(or a candidate's job matches);

:Each result carries its archetype + scoringProfile;

if (How to present?) then (mixed pool)
  :Default to a FAIR-COMPARISON lens;
  note right
    Do not rank students directly against
    seniors on one number. Offer either:
    * separate "early-career pipeline" view, or
    * a normalized view that compares within band
  end note
else (single archetype)
  :Rank within the shared scoring profile;
endif

partition "Match card (archetype-aware)" {
  :Badge: BAU / STUDENT-GRADUATE / CAREER-SWITCHER\n+ availability date (e.g. "free from July");
  :Match score WITH its confidence band\n(not a false-precise single number);
  :For students: POTENTIAL / READINESS score\nshown alongside the skills match;
  :Evidence with PROVENANCE labels\n(academic project vs production job vs self-declared);
  :Strengths · learnable gaps (not "missing -> reject");
  :Interview probes\n(validate self-declared & project skills);
  :Assumptions / imputations made\n(so the recruiter can judge the uncertainty);
}

:Recruiter can drill into evidence + open artifact links\n(GitHub / demo / thesis);
:Recruiter decision\n(advance / interview / pass), with reasons captured;

note right
  The recruiter's core need for a student: SEE that a low
  "experience" number is structural, not a red flag, and get
  the evidence + probes to assess potential fairly. Transparency
  about provenance and assumptions is what makes it fair.
end note
stop
@enduml
